      "body": "**Why.** With sequence parallelism, `LLaVAModel._process_embedding_token_parallel` split the combined text and image embeddings with `scatter_to_sequence_parallel_region` and no group, which means the global TP group. The language model it feeds is built on `self.pg_collection.tp`. A LLaVA model given a collection that differs from the global grid kept the wrong sequence chunk on each rank, and the backward all-gather collected gradients from the wrong ranks.\n\n**What.** Pass `self.pg_collection.tp` to the scatter.\n\n**Tests.** The new `tests/unit_tests/models/test_llava_process_groups.py` gives the model its own TP=2 groups while the global grid has TP=1, and makes the global TP accessors raise. It checks the chunk each rank keeps and the gradient gathered in backward. The test fails on main and passes here on 4 GPUs. `test_llava_model.py` and `test_llava_training.py` give the same results as on main.\n\n**Compatibility.** No change on the standard grid, where `self.pg_collection.tp` is the global TP group.\n\nPart of #6307.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
